    <innernamespace refid="namespacehorus__generator__pattern">horus_generator_pattern</innernamespace>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Manual generator: the device follows targets sent by the operator (UI joint sliders). </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Targets arrive as sensor_msgs/JointState on <computeroutput>topic</computeroutput> (names + position, or + effort for <computeroutput>quantity: effort</computeroutput>); joints not named keep their target. The output moves toward the target at most <computeroutput>max_rate</computeroutput> per second (rad/s or N m/s), so a slider jump is a ramp, never a step. Position output starts at the measured pose; effort output starts at zero. With no target for <computeroutput>timeout</computeroutput> s the target freezes at the current output (hold). Continuous: runs until the behavior is canceled.</para>
<para>manual: plugin: horus_generator_pattern/Manual joints: [hipR, kneeR, ankleR] quantity: position # position | effort max_rate: 0.5 # rad/s (position) or N m/s (effort) min: [-0.5, 0.0, -0.3] # optional clamp per joint (default: none) max: [ 0.8, 1.2, 0.3] timeout: 1.0 # s without a target -&gt; hold topic: ~/manual_target </para>
    </detaileddescription>
